    "turn_text": "Let's get your take, Robert, on this, because I think it's very, very important. First of all, I'm you as glad as we are that they took it up. I think it is of great consequence and constitutional importance. And how do you think the argument should go? Do you believe in this broad immunity, which I felt that that was a little bit of a stretch, for example, we have freedom of speech, but you can't, you know, scream fire in a crowded theater. and create a panic at that point. So there's a certain limitation in that respect. I would imagine that there is a way to thread the needle where a president would be able to get advice, make controversial decisions as president with the authority as president, as the with the authority as commander in chief. However, it wouldn't include sending out a sealed team six group to go kill your political opponent.",
